---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Cta from "../../components/Cta.astro";
import { platforms } from "../../config";
const kalshi = platforms.find((p) => p.id === "kalshi")!;

const howToSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  name: "How to use Kalshi: sign up and place your first trade",
  step: [
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Create your account" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Verify your identity" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Add funds" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Find a market" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Place your first trade" },
  ],
};
---

<Base
  title="How to use Kalshi (step-by-step)"
  description="A beginner's step-by-step guide to signing up for Kalshi, funding your account, and placing your first prediction-market trade."
  path="/guides/how-to-use-kalshi"
  schema={howToSchema}
>
  <article class="prose wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
    <h1>How to use Kalshi: your first trade</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Kalshi is the most beginner-friendly regulated option for US residents.
      Here's the whole process, start to finish: it takes about 10 minutes.
    </p>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Create your account.</strong> Sign up with your email and a
        password. You'll need to be 18+ and a US resident.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Verify your identity.</strong> Because Kalshi is regulated, you'll
        confirm your identity (a standard KYC step, like opening a bank account).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Add funds.</strong> Link a bank account or debit card and deposit a
        small amount to start: even $10 is fine.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Find a market.</strong> Browse categories (economics, politics,
        weather, sports). Each market is a yes/no question with a live price.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Place your first trade.</strong> Pick "Yes" or "No", choose how many
        contracts, and confirm. Your potential profit and loss are shown before you
        commit.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Beginner tip.</strong> Start tiny. Place one small trade just to see
      how the whole cycle works: buying, watching the price, and settlement: before
      putting in more.
    </div>

    <h2>Ready to start?</h2>
    <Cta platform={kalshi} />

    <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--ink-soft); margin-top:1.5rem;">
      Educational content only, not financial advice. Only trade with money you can
      afford to lose. Availability and rules depend on your location and age.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
